One container issue per Start work request (migration 0097)

Adds migration 0097, a partial unique index on the issues table (company_id, origin_id) that only applies to rows whose origin_kind is 'start_work' and whose origin_id is set. The Start work dialog will give every typed request one key and the planner will store it in origin_id, so this index guarantees one request key can only ever produce one container issue, even if the person presses Enter twice, a request dies halfway, or two tabs or two server processes submit the same key. On purpose the index ignores status and hidden_at, unlike the recovery indexes from migration 0070, so a rejected (cancelled) container keeps its key and a retry after reject hands back the rejected plan instead of drafting a new one. It is additive, uses IF NOT EXISTS, cannot fail on existing data because no start_work rows exist yet, and rolls back by dropping the one index. The same index is mirrored in the drizzle schema as startWorkRequestIdx, the journal gains entry 97, and a 0097 snapshot chained to 0096 was generated so drizzle-kit reports no schema drift. Verified by building the db package, drizzle 'No schema changes', the migration numbering check, the db client migration suite against embedded Postgres (which applies 0097 and replays it), and a clean typecheck. Not applied to any database.

